WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.147
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.417 --> 00:07.626
Man, I feel so bad for Byeong Nam.

3
00:07.626 --> 00:09.426
Isn't that usually late Private First Class or early Corporal?

4
00:09.426 --> 00:10.928
Exactly.

5
00:10.928 --> 00:13.584
Why dump a guy who's about to get discharged?

6
00:13.584 --> 00:15.709
That's why you rookies don't know anything.

7
00:15.709 --> 00:17.518
What month is it?

8
00:17.518 --> 00:18.876
September!

9
00:18.876 --> 00:20.395
Keep it down!

10
00:20.395 --> 00:22.648
- September. - Right. It's September, yeah?

11
00:22.648 --> 00:24.233
So what season is September?

12
00:24.233 --> 00:25.734
Chuseok?

13
00:26.751 --> 00:29.000
- Harvest season? - Harvest season, my ass.

14
00:29.000 --> 00:32.042
Fall semester, idiot. What happens then?

15
00:32.042 --> 00:34.792
What happens?

16
00:34.792 --> 00:36.954
Well...

17
00:36.954 --> 00:38.956
That's when the returning students come back.

18
00:38.956 --> 00:41.333
- Returning students. Huh? - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! Right!

19
00:41.333 --> 00:45.125
Those damn hyenas have discharge papers, unlike us!

20
00:45.125 --> 00:47.005
What do you think they do with those guys?

21
00:47.005 --> 00:48.459
Go to the semester kickoff party.

22
00:48.459 --> 00:51.593
What's a semester kickoff party?

23
00:51.593 --> 00:52.886
Well...

24
00:52.886 --> 00:55.055
It's a start-of-semester party.

25
00:55.055 --> 00:57.182
- Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! - A start-of-semester party. Got it?

26
00:57.182 --> 00:58.767
And once they get there,

27
00:58.767 --> 01:01.228
instead of grunts like us,

28
01:01.228 --> 01:04.523
there are polished guys who've already been discharged,

29
01:04.523 --> 01:06.959
with their hair slicked back with pomade,

30
01:06.959 --> 01:10.279
rolling up in imported cars, looking cool as hell.

31
01:10.279 --> 01:13.198
Then they casually sling an arm round her like a grown man and go,

32
01:13.198 --> 01:15.117
"Bit Na Ri, need anything?"

33
01:15.117 --> 01:16.809
Yes, I do!

34
01:17.537 --> 01:19.372
- Don't overdo it. - Sorry.

35
01:19.372 --> 01:20.581
If a guy asks her that, huh?

36
01:20.581 --> 01:22.833
Wouldn't you be tempted too?

37
01:22.833 --> 01:23.960
- We would... - We would...

38
01:23.960 --> 01:26.170
That's why September has always been

39
01:26.170 --> 01:30.168
a rough month for guys in the military.

40
01:30.168 --> 01:33.761
I heard this from my seniors when I was a brand-new Private.

41
01:33.761 --> 01:36.722
There was this crazy senior named Lee Ho Chang. I think he was a Corporal.

42
01:36.722 --> 01:38.933
His girlfriend sent him a photo.

43
01:38.933 --> 01:41.394
She was all dressed up in a beautiful hanbok...

44
01:41.394 --> 01:43.959
but she had her rubber shoes on backward.

45
01:43.959 --> 01:45.606
Isn't that just cruel?

46
01:45.606 --> 01:47.316
Hey, this is about one of my buddies.

47
01:47.316 --> 01:50.001
He got a letter from his girlfriend, and there was nothing written in it.

48
01:50.001 --> 01:52.363
Just two stars drawn on the page.

49
01:52.363 --> 01:54.073
What does that mean?

50
01:54.073 --> 01:55.282
Two stars...

51
01:55.282 --> 01:56.659
Two stars?

52
01:56.659 --> 01:58.243
A breakup!

53
02:00.418 --> 02:04.125
Byeong Nam must be completely crushed right now.

54
02:04.125 --> 02:05.751
You guys need to look after him.

55
02:05.751 --> 02:07.670
First, get him taken off guard duty.

56
02:07.670 --> 02:10.042
If he goes on duty right now, he might actually shoot someone.

57
02:10.042 --> 02:11.132
- Understood. - Yes, understood.

58
02:11.132 --> 02:12.925
Treat him like he's on a two-week watch and keep an eye on him.

59
02:12.925 --> 02:14.844
And make sure he always has a buddy with him.

60
02:14.844 --> 02:15.845
- Yes, understood. - Yes, understood.

61
02:15.845 --> 02:18.097
You look after him too. Don't give him a hard time for no reason.

62
02:18.097 --> 02:20.474
- I won't even let him touch a gun. - Okay. Good.

63
02:20.474 --> 02:22.334
Now hurry up and go take care

64
02:22.334 --> 02:24.228
- of Choi Byeong Nam. - Yes, understood.

65
02:24.228 --> 02:25.229
All right, dismissed!

66
02:25.229 --> 02:27.588
- Yes, understood! - Let's go.

67
02:41.329 --> 02:42.376
What?

68
02:42.376 --> 02:44.582
You didn't even eat breakfast. You're not eating this either?

69
02:44.582 --> 02:46.459
He wouldn't even touch the seaweed soup or sausage stir-fry.

70
02:46.459 --> 02:47.835
This is really serious.

71
02:47.835 --> 02:52.476
At least have some of your favorite beef-bone soup ramen.

72
02:53.424 --> 02:55.134
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam...

73
02:55.134 --> 02:58.137
We made your beef-bone soup ramen. Why won't you eat it?

74
02:58.137 --> 03:01.348
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam, please eat this.

75
03:02.183 --> 03:03.809
Did he go mute?

76
03:03.809 --> 03:04.835
Looks like it.

77
03:04.835 --> 03:05.853
This could last a while.

78
03:05.853 --> 03:08.147
Shouldn't we ask Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu for help?

79
03:08.147 --> 03:10.733
He gets dumped all the time. How would he help?

80
03:10.733 --> 03:13.918
That's exactly why he'd know what to do.

81
03:13.918 --> 03:15.071
- Right? - Yes.

82
03:15.071 --> 03:16.322
Oh, right.

83
03:16.322 --> 03:17.740
Who had the last guard shift yesterday?

84
03:17.740 --> 03:20.242
- Corporal Ji Jeong Min! - I heard you screwed up on guard duty.

85
03:20.242 --> 03:21.327
On guard duty?

86
03:21.327 --> 03:22.668
Yeah. I heard you didn't do the suha challenge.

87
03:22.668 --> 03:25.585
I heard you didn't do the suha challenge.

88
03:25.585 --> 03:27.875
- Oh, suha... - Su Ah?

89
03:27.875 --> 03:30.877
I heard the officer on duty chewed you out for not doing the suha challenge properly.

90
03:30.877 --> 03:32.546
Su Ah...

91
03:32.546 --> 03:33.585
Is Bang Su Ah your girlfriend?

92
03:33.585 --> 03:35.220
Yes, she is!

93
03:45.877 --> 03:47.645
Hey, snap out of it.

94
03:47.645 --> 03:48.938
Corporal Kim Dong Woo...

95
03:48.938 --> 03:50.439
You think skipping the challenge on guard duty is a joke?

96
03:50.439 --> 03:52.386
It wasn't a joke!

97
03:55.152 --> 03:57.334
My feelings for Su Ah... They weren't a joke. I really loved her!

98
03:57.334 --> 03:58.959
Why are you doing this?

99
03:58.959 --> 04:00.491
What on earth do you know?

100
04:00.491 --> 04:01.585
Do you know anything about love?

101
04:01.585 --> 04:03.959
That's not what I meant...

102
04:05.585 --> 04:07.501
Su Ah...

103
04:07.501 --> 04:09.849
- Su Ah... - Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

104
04:12.168 --> 04:14.929
Well, at least he's talking again.

105
04:15.756 --> 04:16.877
Chungseong! Love you!

106
04:16.877 --> 04:17.925
Love you too.

107
04:17.925 --> 04:19.635
- What's up? - Well...

108
04:19.635 --> 04:22.190
I think you should take a look at this.

109
04:26.117 --> 04:29.353
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam has been reading books he normally wouldn't,

110
04:29.353 --> 04:32.501
and he keeps repeating his girlfriend's name.

111
04:32.501 --> 04:36.168
I think he may be having some dangerous thoughts.

112
04:36.168 --> 04:38.712
- Yoon Mo. - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

113
04:41.824 --> 04:43.951
Yes, understood.

114
04:43.951 --> 04:45.494
[Soldier requiring special attention]

115
04:45.494 --> 04:48.622
You know a soldier who needs extra attention should get it, right?

116
04:48.622 --> 04:49.710
Yes, I understand.

117
04:49.710 --> 04:52.204
- Keep a close eye on him. - Yes, understood!

118
05:02.094 --> 05:03.387
Hello.

119
05:03.387 --> 05:05.890
I'd like to request a visit.

120
05:05.890 --> 05:08.517
Yes, please fill this out.

121
05:08.517 --> 05:10.811
Okay, thank you.

122
05:13.063 --> 05:17.419
[Visitor Application Form] [Name: Jeon Woo Ju, Relation: Sister]

123
05:19.779 --> 05:22.042
[Jeon Se Gye]

124
05:22.042 --> 05:23.532
Here it is.

125
05:23.532 --> 05:25.033
Thank you.

126
05:26.410 --> 05:28.412
You're here to see Jeon Se Gye.

127
05:28.412 --> 05:29.413
Yes.

128
05:29.413 --> 05:31.123
And you're his older sister.

129
05:31.123 --> 05:34.585
- Yes. - Sister... Jeon Se Gye...

130
05:34.585 --> 05:36.754
Jeon Se Gye's sister?

131
05:36.754 --> 05:39.215
Yes, Jeon Se Gye's sister, Jeon Woo Ju.

132
05:39.215 --> 05:41.026
Nice to meet you.

133
05:53.228 --> 05:55.478
- Thank you. - Yes.

134
05:56.982 --> 06:00.459
[EP07. Woo Ju like you]

135
06:00.459 --> 06:01.821
Who is she?

136
06:01.821 --> 06:05.921
I think she's the most beautiful woman I've ever seen.

137
06:08.084 --> 06:09.918
- Are you okay? - She's beautiful...

138
06:09.918 --> 06:11.501
- What? - Huh?

139
06:11.501 --> 06:14.375
I almost got completely mesmerized.

140
06:14.375 --> 06:15.417
Who is she?

141
06:15.417 --> 06:17.444
Can't you tell just by looking?

142
06:17.444 --> 06:19.893
She's Jeon Se Gye's sister.

143
06:20.631 --> 06:22.168
No wonder they look exactly alike.

144
06:22.168 --> 06:24.927
Put her in a uniform, and she'd look just like Jeon Se Gye.

145
06:24.927 --> 06:26.525
[Norwegian Wood]

146
06:27.334 --> 06:29.348
Would it have been better to send him out on work detail?

147
06:29.348 --> 06:31.183
What a thing to happen right at the end of his service.

148
06:31.183 --> 06:34.334
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam, maybe ease up on all this loss.

149
06:34.334 --> 06:36.564
Isn't that "losing it" more than "loss?"

150
06:36.564 --> 06:40.084
I don't think he can hear a single thing.

151
06:40.084 --> 06:42.111
Choi Byeong Nam, cheer up.

152
06:42.111 --> 06:44.405
We'll be home before long.

153
06:44.405 --> 06:46.282
Announcement from the admin office.

154
06:46.282 --> 06:48.325
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye, report to the admin office.

155
06:48.325 --> 06:49.380
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye,

156
06:49.380 --> 06:51.412
- please report to the admin office. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

157
06:51.412 --> 06:54.081
- Heading to the admin office. - Sure, what, another event?

158
06:54.081 --> 06:56.250
Not sure. I'll be right back.

159
06:56.250 --> 06:57.293
Okay.

160
06:57.293 --> 06:59.377
- See you. - Yes.

161
06:59.377 --> 07:01.418
Is he going to run off or something?

162
07:01.418 --> 07:03.465
If he were going to desert, he'd have done it ages ago.

163
07:03.465 --> 07:05.465
The kid's a total chicken, no way.

164
07:06.469 --> 07:08.137
He looks serious.

165
07:08.137 --> 07:10.723
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye, reporting to the admin office.

166
07:10.723 --> 07:11.724
Hey, Se Gye.

167
07:11.724 --> 07:13.768
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

168
07:13.768 --> 07:15.884
So, how do I put this...

169
07:17.084 --> 07:18.168
What is it?

170
07:18.168 --> 07:20.155
Your sister's here to visit.

171
07:21.001 --> 07:22.318
- Oh, really? - Yeah,

172
07:22.318 --> 07:24.194
- get ready and head out. - Yes, understood.

173
07:24.194 --> 07:25.821
Chungseong! Love you!

174
07:25.821 --> 07:27.114
Yeah, love you too.

175
07:27.114 --> 07:28.865
- Take care. - Bye now.

176
07:31.918 --> 07:34.872
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye, back from the admin office.

177
07:34.872 --> 07:36.290
Why'd they call you?

178
07:36.290 --> 07:38.917
Oh, they said my sister came to visit.

179
07:38.917 --> 07:39.835
- Sister? - Sister?

180
07:39.835 --> 07:41.045
Yes, that's right.

181
07:41.045 --> 07:42.880
Okay, hurry up and get ready and head out.

182
07:42.880 --> 07:44.795
Yes, understood.

183
07:45.835 --> 07:47.509
- Se Gye. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

184
07:47.509 --> 07:49.887
Your sister, is that the one in the photo you showed us before?

185
07:49.887 --> 07:51.638
Yes, that's right.

186
07:52.918 --> 07:55.392
What's your sister's type, brother-in-law?

187
07:55.392 --> 07:59.229
She likes tall, gentle guys like you.

188
07:59.229 --> 08:02.274
She was in the US for work and came back to Korea a little while ago.

189
08:02.274 --> 08:04.610
She looks just like him but way prettier, right?

190
08:04.610 --> 08:06.710
Come on, not that much.

191
08:06.710 --> 08:09.698
Hey, mind if I tag along?

192
08:09.698 --> 08:11.408
- Come with me. - Really?

193
08:11.408 --> 08:12.993
Hey, why would you go along?

194
08:12.993 --> 08:17.122
She's Se Gye's sister, it'd be nice to say hello.

195
08:17.122 --> 08:19.167
Fine! Then I'm coming too.

196
08:19.167 --> 08:20.167
Sounds good.

197
08:20.167 --> 08:22.836
He's meeting his own sister, why are you lot going?

198
08:22.836 --> 08:24.126
You're not coming?

199
08:24.126 --> 08:26.173
No, I'll study.

200
08:26.173 --> 08:27.751
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

201
08:27.751 --> 08:28.759
You're not coming?

202
08:28.759 --> 08:30.552
I'm not going.

203
08:30.552 --> 08:32.805
Corporal Kim Dong Woo, I'll run to the bathroom real quick.

204
08:32.805 --> 08:34.306
Sure, take your time but be quick.

205
08:34.306 --> 08:35.432
Yes, understood.

206
08:35.432 --> 08:37.763
I'll take my time but be quick.

207
08:39.918 --> 08:41.814
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam,

208
08:41.814 --> 08:44.108
come get some fresh air with us.

209
08:44.108 --> 08:45.901
It's barely been any time since the breakup.

210
08:45.901 --> 08:48.112
And Se Gye's sister's ideal type was me.

211
08:48.112 --> 08:49.989
Tall and gentle.

212
08:49.989 --> 08:52.908
I shouldn't go and stir up her feelings for nothing.

213
08:52.908 --> 08:57.204
You mean Se Gye's sister's feelings, not yours?

214
08:57.204 --> 08:59.209
Obviously, you idiot.

215
08:59.209 --> 09:01.834
I'm just not ready to love again yet.

216
09:01.834 --> 09:05.003
But isn't that kind of a pointless worry...

217
09:05.922 --> 09:08.585
Hey, I'm Choi Byeong Nam.

218
09:08.585 --> 09:10.217
A few smooth lines and she'd fall for me fast.

219
09:10.217 --> 09:13.637
Come on, these days it's less about the talk and more about this, right?

220
09:13.637 --> 09:15.001
Guys with good bodies are what's in.

221
09:15.001 --> 09:17.349
I've met a lot of pretty girls, so trust me,

222
09:17.349 --> 09:18.904
you've got to play it cool

223
09:18.904 --> 09:20.436
- to get their attention... - Hey.

224
09:20.436 --> 09:23.647
These days, women like soft-looking guys. Guys like me...

225
09:23.647 --> 09:25.024
What? You laughing?

226
09:25.024 --> 09:26.751
Soft-looking? More like fermented tofu.

227
09:26.751 --> 09:28.376
Silken tofu.

228
09:28.376 --> 09:29.695
Forget tofu.

229
09:29.695 --> 09:33.580
A man wins women over with his eyes.

230
09:33.580 --> 09:35.534
Man, I should be studying...

231
09:35.534 --> 09:37.327
Do I really have to show you guys?

232
09:37.327 --> 09:41.049
I'll put my studying on hold today and teach you instead.

233
09:42.041 --> 09:45.168
Well, if that's what we're doing, I'll show you how it's done.

234
09:45.168 --> 09:47.796
Hey, let's step out for some fresh air.

235
09:47.796 --> 09:49.006
I'm really fine.

236
09:49.006 --> 09:51.216
Come on, let's go together and say hello.

237
09:51.216 --> 09:52.509
I said I'm fine.

238
09:52.509 --> 09:55.665
It's a bit awkward for us to go on our own.

239
10:10.611 --> 10:14.001
Wait, you already changed?

240
10:14.001 --> 10:15.543
Change slowly.

241
10:15.543 --> 10:17.376
I'll change quickly!

242
10:17.376 --> 10:19.744
- Hurry up and change. - Yes! Understood!

243
10:21.293 --> 10:23.707
Hold on, isn't that your A-class uniform?

244
10:23.707 --> 10:25.438
It's S-class.

245
10:29.671 --> 10:30.877
Take it over there!

246
10:30.877 --> 10:32.501
Sorry.

247
10:32.501 --> 10:34.585
His voice has got some power in it now.

248
10:34.585 --> 10:36.595
An age of loss...

249
10:38.376 --> 10:40.209
Chungseong! Love you!

250
10:40.209 --> 10:41.808
Keep up the good work.

251
10:42.601 --> 10:44.165
[Norwegian Wood]

252
10:46.209 --> 10:48.565
Are you sure he is okay?

253
10:48.565 --> 10:50.109
Maybe we shouldn't have dragged him here.

254
10:50.109 --> 10:52.319
It's better than leaving him alone.

255
10:52.319 --> 10:53.779
Right.

256
10:53.779 --> 10:57.783
Maybe some good food will cheer him up.

257
10:57.783 --> 11:00.001
If this keeps up, he's really going to lose it.

258
11:00.001 --> 11:01.632
Okay, let's go.

259
11:02.232 --> 11:04.622
- First Sergeant? - Yeah?

260
11:04.622 --> 11:08.293
I heard Se Gye's sister is visiting. Who's escorting her?

261
11:08.293 --> 11:10.254
Good question. What should we do?

262
11:10.254 --> 11:13.674
I heard she's really beautiful. Maybe we could...

263
11:13.674 --> 11:16.970
Beautiful, my ass. I bet my daughter's prettier.

264
11:17.678 --> 11:20.014
Platoon Leader, perfect timing.

265
11:20.014 --> 11:23.392
Jeon Sekai's sister is here to visit, so could you show her in?

266
11:23.392 --> 11:26.478
- All right. - Oh, did you hear?

267
11:26.478 --> 11:28.993
Apparently, she's gorgeous.

268
11:32.918 --> 11:36.280
Is that so? But that doesn't really concern me.

269
11:36.280 --> 11:38.157
Well, that's new.

270
11:38.157 --> 11:39.283
You're not overreacting.

271
11:39.283 --> 11:44.126
Actually, my heart already belongs to another woman.

272
11:44.126 --> 11:45.622
If you'll excuse me.

273
11:46.835 --> 11:48.084
I don't know what that was,

274
11:48.084 --> 11:49.668
but he's found a whole new way to overreact.

275
11:49.668 --> 11:50.793
That's right.

276
11:50.793 --> 11:52.502
- Let's go. - Yes.

277
11:59.137 --> 12:00.334
Hey, Sung Yoon Mo!

278
12:00.334 --> 12:02.334
- Corporal Sung Yoon Mo. - Aren't you coming?

279
12:02.334 --> 12:03.348
Yes, sir.

280
12:03.348 --> 12:04.548
[Military notebook]

281
12:30.000 --> 12:31.394
Woo Ju!

282
12:34.546 --> 12:36.488
Se Gye!

283
12:59.696 --> 13:00.697
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam!

284
13:00.697 --> 13:02.488
Where are you going?

285
13:03.825 --> 13:04.868
Where is he going?

286
13:04.868 --> 13:06.042
He's so fast.

287
13:06.042 --> 13:07.463
He's ridiculously fast.

288
13:10.666 --> 13:11.877
Was it hard getting here?

289
13:11.877 --> 13:13.042
Yeah. Have you been well?

290
13:13.042 --> 13:15.470
Of course. Come on.

291
13:20.092 --> 13:22.155
Attention, troops!

292
13:22.761 --> 13:24.887
The goddess in white has arrived.

293
13:24.887 --> 13:28.058
Salute Se Gye's stunningly beautiful sister!

294
13:28.058 --> 13:29.643
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

295
13:29.643 --> 13:30.769
Love you...

296
13:30.769 --> 13:32.646
Chungseong. Love you.

297
13:32.646 --> 13:34.564
Love you.

298
13:34.564 --> 13:35.857
She says she loves us!

299
13:35.857 --> 13:37.567
Love!

300
13:37.567 --> 13:38.860
Sis, let's sit down.

301
13:38.860 --> 13:40.957
Please, take a seat, everyone.

302
13:46.535 --> 13:49.288
- Here you go. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

303
13:49.288 --> 13:50.793
Then my duty here is done.

304
13:50.793 --> 13:52.624
Thank you.

305
13:52.624 --> 13:54.197
Thank you, sir.

306
14:01.091 --> 14:03.593
So, who is everyone?

307
14:03.593 --> 14:06.585
They're the senior guys in my barracks.

308
14:06.585 --> 14:10.902
Hi. I'm Jeon Woo Ju, Se Gye's sister.

309
14:14.877 --> 14:18.066
- Is everyone all right? - Huh?

310
14:18.066 --> 14:20.597
Of course. I'm doing great.

311
14:21.585 --> 14:23.322
Could you introduce us?

312
14:23.322 --> 14:24.614
Of course.

313
14:24.614 --> 14:26.908
Starting here, this is Sergeant Kang Chan Seok.

314
14:26.908 --> 14:29.077
The one who ran off earlier is Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

315
14:29.077 --> 14:31.830
- And this is our squad leader, Corporal Kim. - Corporal Kim Dong Woo.

316
14:31.830 --> 14:33.582
- This is Corporal Cha Byeong Ho. - Corporal Cha Byeong Ho.

317
14:33.582 --> 14:35.959
- And Corporal Ji Jeong Min. - Corporal Ji Jeong Min.

318
14:35.959 --> 14:38.337
- Nice to meet you. - Nice to meet you.

319
14:38.337 --> 14:42.835
Wait. Other than Se Gye, you're all sergeants and corporals.

320
14:42.835 --> 14:44.469
Yeah, that's right.

321
14:45.469 --> 14:48.293
Everyone's okay... right?

322
14:48.293 --> 14:51.585
They're all just a little shy.

323
14:51.585 --> 14:54.402
Come on. We're not shy.

324
15:03.251 --> 15:05.238
Hey, he's completely out of it.

325
15:05.238 --> 15:06.877
Corporal Ji Jeong Min, are you okay?

326
15:06.877 --> 15:08.168
Corporal Ji Jeong Min!

327
15:08.168 --> 15:10.126
He must work out a lot.

328
15:10.126 --> 15:11.537
He's really strong.

329
15:11.537 --> 15:13.212
I like...

330
15:18.001 --> 15:19.669
Hey! Ease up!

331
15:19.669 --> 15:20.835
Hey, Cha Byeong Ho!

332
15:20.835 --> 15:23.358
- Snap out of it. - Thank you.

333
15:23.965 --> 15:26.996
Oh, squad leader. You're so charismatic.

334
15:27.668 --> 15:30.847
But you also have this soft, gentle look.

335
15:30.847 --> 15:33.433
I bet women love your look.

336
15:33.433 --> 15:36.674
I bet women love your look.

337
15:39.959 --> 15:41.566
- Kim Dong Woo! - Corporal Kim Dong Woo!

338
15:41.566 --> 15:43.610
You're making her uncomfortable.

339
15:43.610 --> 15:46.626
Yes. Sorry. Thank you.

340
15:46.626 --> 15:49.199
Did you buy all this?

341
15:49.199 --> 15:52.536
I didn't buy it. They said I shouldn't come to a visit empty-handed,

342
15:52.536 --> 15:56.248
- so I made everything myself. - Really?

343
15:56.248 --> 15:58.333
- This took forever to make! - What's with him all of a sudden?

344
15:58.333 --> 16:00.042
I realized I had a chance.

345
16:00.042 --> 16:02.971
I told you. A tall, sensitive guy...

346
16:03.585 --> 16:04.626
Hello.

347
16:04.626 --> 16:06.418
Oh, you're back.

348
16:06.418 --> 16:08.593
Here, try some of this,

349
16:08.593 --> 16:10.179
Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

350
16:10.179 --> 16:12.154
- Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam. - Choi Byeong Nam...

351
16:12.154 --> 16:14.350
Oh, you're back. Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

352
16:14.350 --> 16:17.144
- Choi Byeong Nam... - Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam.

353
16:17.144 --> 16:18.835
Choi Byeong Nam...

354
16:18.835 --> 16:20.438
Please snap out of it.

355
16:20.438 --> 16:23.209
I thought I heard an angel's voice.

356
16:23.209 --> 16:25.068
When did you learn to bake like this?

357
16:25.068 --> 16:28.319
I tried, but I'm not sure how it turned out.

358
16:30.324 --> 16:32.015
What?

359
16:32.710 --> 16:34.369
There was nothing for him to latch onto.

360
16:34.369 --> 16:36.663
I think he's just letting his imagination run wild.

361
16:36.663 --> 16:38.828
What exactly did you latch onto?

362
16:38.828 --> 16:41.418
Oh, sorry.

363
16:41.418 --> 16:43.837
Please eat up even if they aren't very good.

364
16:43.837 --> 16:46.042
I like men with big appetites.

365
16:46.042 --> 16:47.668
A man with a big appetite...

366
16:47.668 --> 16:49.543
Please slow down. You'll choke.

367
16:49.543 --> 16:51.887
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, I'll take this one.

368
16:51.887 --> 16:53.710
I'm not giving that up.

369
16:53.710 --> 16:55.251
Delicious!

370
16:55.251 --> 16:57.175
Here's some juice. Please have some.

371
16:59.126 --> 17:00.540
So good.

372
17:05.459 --> 17:08.329
- She's beautiful. - Try some of this!

373
17:09.279 --> 17:10.859
No... I can't!

374
17:11.459 --> 17:13.206
Yoo Bin...

375
17:17.501 --> 17:19.158
She's beautiful...

376
17:20.751 --> 17:22.396
Yoo Bin...

377
17:23.585 --> 17:26.727
I can eat and eat without ever getting full.

378
17:29.501 --> 17:30.967
I really enjoyed that.

379
17:30.967 --> 17:33.512
Thank you for enjoying the food.

380
17:33.512 --> 17:35.501
We're going outside for some fresh air.

381
17:35.501 --> 17:37.273
Okay.

382
17:38.601 --> 17:40.185
You can leave everything. I'll clean up.

383
17:40.185 --> 17:41.751
No, I'll do it.

384
17:41.751 --> 17:44.064
Thank you.

385
17:44.064 --> 17:46.704
- See you later. - Take your time.

386
17:50.501 --> 17:53.198
Man, that was seriously creepy. Ugh, I've got goosebumps!

387
17:53.198 --> 17:56.702
What? I've still got it, right?

388
17:56.702 --> 17:59.454
"Oh, you're so strong."

389
17:59.454 --> 18:01.915
"You have this soft, gentle look. I bet women love your look."

390
18:01.915 --> 18:03.959
"Please eat up even if they aren't very good."

391
18:03.959 --> 18:07.585
"I like men with big appetites."

392
18:07.585 --> 18:08.964
You little brat...

393
18:08.964 --> 18:11.174
You should be thanking me, not making fun of me.

394
18:11.174 --> 18:15.011
I got all dressed up and came here to make your life in the military easier.

395
18:15.011 --> 18:17.430
You'd better appreciate what your pretty sister just did.

396
18:17.430 --> 18:19.808
I was doing just fine without your help.

397
18:19.808 --> 18:21.958
I'm sure you were.

398
18:23.353 --> 18:25.188
Oh, by the way,

399
18:25.188 --> 18:27.459
that half-pickled cucumber from earlier?

400
18:27.459 --> 18:29.668
Then my duty here is done.

401
18:29.668 --> 18:31.194
That's what he looked like.

402
18:31.194 --> 18:33.835
- A pickle. - Is he high-ranking?

403
18:33.835 --> 18:35.365
He's our platoon leader,

404
18:35.365 --> 18:37.418
one of our company's officers.

405
18:37.418 --> 18:39.209
He must be pretty high-ranking.

406
18:39.209 --> 18:40.677
Right.

407
18:43.289 --> 18:44.291
Is there something on my face?

408
18:44.291 --> 18:45.875
- Yeah... - Where?

409
18:45.875 --> 18:48.296
Right there. You've got ugly all over it.

410
18:48.296 --> 18:51.126
What are you talking about? I'm Jeon Se Gye.

411
18:51.126 --> 18:54.718
Exactly. Where did the real Jeon Se Gye go?

412
18:54.718 --> 18:57.012
Hey, Jeon Se Gye. Where are you?

413
18:57.012 --> 18:59.969
Insulting my face is like insulting your own.

414
19:00.918 --> 19:03.468
Hey, do you even wear sunscreen?

415
19:03.468 --> 19:05.059
Why are you so dark?

416
19:05.059 --> 19:07.689
What do you think? It's a military tan. Cool, right?

417
19:07.689 --> 19:09.983
Can't you smell it? The scent of a man.

418
19:09.983 --> 19:11.959
The scent of a soldier.

419
19:11.959 --> 19:13.862
The scent of a manly soldier, my ass.

420
19:13.862 --> 19:16.042
You just look like you got roasted in the sun.

421
19:16.042 --> 19:18.075
What would you know?

422
19:18.075 --> 19:19.911
Excuse me? "You?"

423
19:19.911 --> 19:21.126
What else should I call you?

424
19:21.126 --> 19:23.585
Should I go, "Oh, sis! My dear sister Woo Ju"?

425
19:23.585 --> 19:26.041
Why, you little...

426
19:26.041 --> 19:28.376
Want me to make you call me "sis?"

427
19:28.376 --> 19:30.209
You haven't had a good beating in a while, have you?

428
19:30.209 --> 19:31.543
You beat the crap out of me when we were kids!

429
19:31.543 --> 19:33.506
- Exactly! I ought to... - Stop it!

430
19:33.506 --> 19:36.168
Seriously, stop!

431
19:36.168 --> 19:37.793
Oh, my!

432
19:37.793 --> 19:40.263
Is my little Se Gye thirsty?

433
19:40.263 --> 19:42.680
Want your big sister to get you something?

434
19:43.559 --> 19:45.042
You're so lucky.

435
19:45.042 --> 19:48.453
Your beautiful sister even pats you on the head.

436
19:50.233 --> 19:52.668
Yes, I am...

437
19:52.668 --> 19:54.277
- Se Gye. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

438
19:54.277 --> 19:55.876
Did something happen?

439
19:56.572 --> 19:57.822
Nothing happened.

440
19:57.822 --> 19:59.741
You must've saved the country in a past life.

441
19:59.741 --> 20:01.910
With a sister this beautiful,

442
20:01.910 --> 20:04.626
the whole world must look beautiful to you.

443
20:04.626 --> 20:06.459
Yes. It does...

444
20:06.459 --> 20:07.959
Yes...

445
20:07.959 --> 20:10.109
That's right!

446
20:13.213 --> 20:15.006
I had a great time today.

447
20:15.006 --> 20:18.168
Please take good care of Se Gye from now on.

448
20:18.168 --> 20:20.679
You have nothing to worry about!

449
20:20.679 --> 20:22.389
Attention, troops!

450
20:22.389 --> 20:24.084
Salute Se Gye's sister!

451
20:24.084 --> 20:26.417
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

452
20:27.352 --> 20:29.487
Chungseong! Love you!

453
20:30.314 --> 20:31.846
Order, arms!

454
20:33.358 --> 20:34.443
Get home safe, Woo Ju.

455
20:34.443 --> 20:36.376
- Take care of yourself here. - Okay!

456
20:36.376 --> 20:38.669
- Take care. - Take care.

457
20:40.334 --> 20:42.001
- Bye. - Love you...

458
20:42.001 --> 20:44.327
- Se Gye, you must be so happy. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

459
20:44.327 --> 20:46.079
Could you ask your sister to come again?

460
20:46.079 --> 20:47.084
I'll ask her.

461
20:47.084 --> 20:49.082
Hey, you know I'm getting discharged soon, right?

462
20:49.082 --> 20:50.418
Anyway, let's talk inside.

463
20:50.418 --> 20:53.294
Ask your sister if she thinks I'm the most handsome.

464
20:53.294 --> 20:54.838
I doubt it.

465
20:54.838 --> 20:57.490
Never mind that. Just get me her number...

466
21:01.512 --> 21:05.001
Do I stay loyal or pursue a new love?

467
21:05.001 --> 21:06.684
No.

468
21:06.684 --> 21:08.518
I'm a man of loyalty.

469
21:08.518 --> 21:11.251
Could I betray a woman I've given my heart to? No!

470
21:11.251 --> 21:14.984
But this might be the start of a new love.

471
21:16.543 --> 21:19.018
What am I to do?

472
21:19.710 --> 21:22.449
No. Loyalty.

473
21:22.449 --> 21:24.570
I'll stay loyal.

474
21:28.913 --> 21:30.611
A sudden shower?

475
21:32.418 --> 21:34.464
Wait. Woo Ju probably doesn't have an umbrella.

476
21:35.057 --> 21:37.418
Woo Ju. Wait.

477
21:44.221 --> 21:45.783
Woo Ju!

478
21:47.585 --> 21:48.835
Woo Ju!

479
21:48.835 --> 21:50.543
Woo Ju!

480
21:50.543 --> 21:52.312
Woo Ju!

481
21:52.312 --> 21:53.563
- Here you go. - Okay.

482
21:53.563 --> 21:55.982
- Thank you. Have a good afternoon. - Woo Ju, wait.

483
21:55.982 --> 21:57.865
- Woo Ju! - Woo Ju.

484
22:03.949 --> 22:05.910
Oh, you're here?

485
22:07.376 --> 22:09.322
Mom.

486
22:12.292 --> 22:14.251
Why is it raining so hard?

487
22:14.251 --> 22:15.293
It's pouring.

488
22:15.293 --> 22:16.418
You came too?

489
22:16.418 --> 22:18.588
- How's your brother? That's good. - He's doing great.

490
22:18.588 --> 22:20.405
- Let's go. - Let's eat something.

491
22:23.510 --> 22:26.687
[May this youth shine for the motherland!]

492
22:38.609 --> 22:42.028
Right. It started raining out of nowhere.

493
22:42.028 --> 22:44.405
And she's Private First Class Jeon Se Gye's sister.

494
22:44.405 --> 22:46.295
I couldn't just let her get soaked.

495
22:46.908 --> 22:51.371
I knew there was a reason he wasn't being dramatic earlier.

496
22:51.371 --> 22:53.790
Should I get him a towel?

497
22:53.790 --> 22:55.625
Leave him be.

498
22:55.625 --> 22:58.877
Maybe the rain will knock some sense into him.

499
22:58.877 --> 23:00.046
Let's go.

500
23:00.046 --> 23:01.754
Yes, First Sergeant.

501
23:02.376 --> 23:04.425
Didn't you buy too much?

502
23:04.425 --> 23:06.587
Man, I bought way too much.

503
23:07.638 --> 23:10.083
[Multipurpose Room] The light's still on.

504
23:16.668 --> 23:19.877
I thought he'd quit after a day or two, but he's really going at it.

505
23:19.877 --> 23:21.234
I know.

506
23:21.234 --> 23:23.236
When he first asked to study after lights-out,

507
23:23.236 --> 23:25.685
I wasn't sure he'd stick with it.

508
23:27.170 --> 23:29.200
The college entrance exam?

509
23:29.200 --> 23:30.952
You're thinking of going to college?

510
23:30.952 --> 23:32.579
Yes, sir.

511
23:32.579 --> 23:34.831
I'm not sure how well I'll do,

512
23:34.831 --> 23:36.082
but I'd like to give it a try.

513
23:36.082 --> 23:38.334
Good. Work hard at it.

514
23:38.334 --> 23:40.587
If you need any help, let me know.

515
23:40.587 --> 23:42.748
Not that you ever would, right?

516
23:43.340 --> 23:44.716
I'll let you know if I need anything.

517
23:44.716 --> 23:46.058
Okay.

518
23:48.970 --> 23:53.526
But seriously, if you need any help, let me know.

519
23:54.601 --> 23:56.562
If there's something you don't understand, don't ask me.

520
23:56.562 --> 23:58.630
Ask someone else.

521
23:59.226 --> 24:00.231
Yes, sir.

522
24:00.231 --> 24:01.858
You can do it.

523
24:01.858 --> 24:03.376
Thank you, sir.

524
24:13.632 --> 24:17.172
Estimate. E-S-T-I-M-A-T-E.

525
24:27.959 --> 24:30.131
He kept at it and worked really hard.

526
24:33.376 --> 24:34.390
How's it going?

527
24:34.390 --> 24:35.835
Sir.

528
24:35.835 --> 24:37.268
Chungseong. Love you.

529
24:37.268 --> 24:38.334
Good.

530
24:38.334 --> 24:40.188
I've been keeping at it.

531
24:40.188 --> 24:42.315
If I asked whether studying alone was hard,

532
24:42.315 --> 24:45.026
you'd just say you were fine, wouldn't you?

533
24:45.026 --> 24:46.746
I'm really fine.

534
24:48.238 --> 24:50.782
But you must need something.

535
24:50.782 --> 24:51.991
You know what's great about the army?

536
24:51.991 --> 24:54.827
Some things are impossible to find, but whatever we do have, we have plenty of.

537
24:54.827 --> 24:56.247
- Right? - Yes, sir.

538
24:56.247 --> 24:58.915
Don't you need a teacher?

539
24:58.915 --> 25:01.398
A teacher?

540
25:32.740 --> 25:34.918
Are you sure about your answer to question 26?

541
25:34.918 --> 25:37.036
- Huh? - You spent...

542
25:37.036 --> 25:40.665
quite a while solving the later questions, then came back to question 26.

543
25:40.665 --> 25:42.125
Didn't you?

544
25:42.125 --> 25:43.376
Yeah...

545
25:43.376 --> 25:45.712
If this were the actual college entrance exam and that were the first question,

546
25:45.712 --> 25:48.495
you'd be completely thrown off from the start.

547
25:51.676 --> 25:53.136
Look at this.

548
25:53.136 --> 25:55.263
Even your pulse is all over the place.

549
25:55.263 --> 25:57.682
The heart never lies.

550
25:57.682 --> 25:59.350
What is a test?

551
25:59.350 --> 26:01.060
It's about pushing forward.

552
26:01.060 --> 26:03.896
If you lose your flow and rhythm, you're done for.

553
26:03.896 --> 26:06.524
The answer to question 26? I don't care.

554
26:06.524 --> 26:08.067
All I care about is

555
26:08.067 --> 26:10.153
how you handle this test,

556
26:10.153 --> 26:12.364
how you push through the entire test,

557
26:12.364 --> 26:14.410
and take control of it.

558
26:16.585 --> 26:18.192
The real test...

559
26:18.793 --> 26:20.830
is all about momentum.

560
26:20.830 --> 26:22.540
Momentum.

561
26:22.540 --> 26:24.333
Do you understand?

562
26:24.333 --> 26:26.668
So... what's the answer to this one?

563
26:26.668 --> 26:28.838
The answer? I don't care.

564
26:28.838 --> 26:30.465
All I care about is whether you...

565
26:30.465 --> 26:32.550
push your way through this entire test,

566
26:32.550 --> 26:33.718
take control of it,

567
26:33.718 --> 26:35.762
and crush it.

568
26:35.762 --> 26:37.181
That's all I care about.

569
26:37.181 --> 26:39.933
Wait. You don't know the answer, do you?

570
26:39.933 --> 26:41.418
I don't care.

571
26:41.418 --> 26:45.566
All I care about is whether you can crush this test.

572
26:46.501 --> 26:48.668
I'm right, aren't I? Huh?

573
26:48.668 --> 26:50.251
You jerk...

574
26:50.251 --> 26:51.987
Why are you doing this?

575
26:51.987 --> 26:53.168
No, seriously...

576
26:53.168 --> 26:55.418
I have to tutor you, or I'll be stuck on tennis duty.

577
26:55.418 --> 26:56.742
You really need to crush this exam.

578
26:56.742 --> 26:58.293
How am I supposed to crush it when you can't?

579
26:58.293 --> 27:00.369
There's a real teacher besides me.

580
27:00.369 --> 27:02.626
- Where is he? - A real teacher.

581
27:02.626 --> 27:08.169
This system of linear equations has exactly one solution

582
27:08.169 --> 27:09.754
if and only if k isn't a.

583
27:09.754 --> 27:11.631
You need to find the real value of a.

584
27:11.631 --> 27:15.134
The condition for it to have exactly one solution

585
27:15.134 --> 27:19.430
is the same as the condition for the matrix above to have an inverse.

586
27:19.430 --> 27:22.600
ad minus bc cannot equal zero.

587
27:22.600 --> 27:26.896
Therefore, negative two k minus one times three

588
27:26.896 --> 27:29.190
cannot equal zero.

589
27:29.190 --> 27:31.609
So negative two k cannot equal three.

590
27:31.609 --> 27:33.484
That makes the answer choice one.

591
27:34.654 --> 27:36.239
That's Hanguk University for you.

592
27:36.239 --> 27:37.657
You really are something else.

593
27:37.657 --> 27:40.076
Thank you. Now try it yourself.

594
27:40.076 --> 27:44.163
So this problem has exactly one solution,

595
27:44.163 --> 27:46.207
but I didn't understand any of that.

596
27:46.207 --> 27:48.267
Could you explain it one more time?

597
27:53.548 --> 27:55.550
I'll explain it again.

598
27:55.550 --> 27:58.302
The answer to a math problem is in the problem itself.

599
27:58.302 --> 28:02.098
The necessary and sufficient condition for a unique solution is the clue.

600
28:02.098 --> 28:05.101
Having exactly one solution is

601
28:05.101 --> 28:08.396
equivalent to the matrix above having an inverse.

602
28:08.396 --> 28:11.858
ad minus bc cannot equal zero.

603
28:11.858 --> 28:13.860
Negative two k cannot equal three.

604
28:13.860 --> 28:16.279
k cannot equal negative three over two.

605
28:16.279 --> 28:18.676
That's why the answer is choice one.

606
28:20.241 --> 28:22.243
Try solving it again.

607
28:22.243 --> 28:25.798
Oh, so ab minus dc...

608
28:27.915 --> 28:29.750
It's d, not b.

609
28:29.750 --> 28:32.111
It's ad minus bc.

610
28:33.257 --> 28:36.132
Right. ad.

611
28:36.132 --> 28:39.218
- So, ab minus dc... - It's d, not b.

612
28:39.218 --> 28:42.388
Why do you keep saying b instead of d?

613
28:42.388 --> 28:43.389
Repeat after me.

614
28:43.389 --> 28:45.600
ad minus bc does not equal zero.

615
28:45.600 --> 28:47.643
ad minus bc does not equal zero.

616
28:47.643 --> 28:50.605
Louder. ad minus bc does not equal zero.

617
28:50.605 --> 28:52.835
ad minus bc does not equal zero.

618
28:52.835 --> 28:53.858
Try solving it again.

619
28:53.858 --> 28:57.904
- ab minus... - Didn't I tell you it's d, not b?

620
28:57.904 --> 29:00.698
Why do you keep saying b instead of d?

621
29:00.698 --> 29:03.242
It's "ad minus bc does not equal zero."

622
29:03.242 --> 29:04.977
Not b.

623
29:07.288 --> 29:08.623
Hey.

624
29:08.623 --> 29:11.000
Since when did you get so angry?

625
29:11.000 --> 29:14.003
If you get mad and sigh at me one more time, you're dead.

626
29:14.003 --> 29:17.809
I'm the teacher, and you're the student.

627
29:27.443 --> 29:30.269
I'm a sergeant, and you're a Private First Class!

628
29:30.269 --> 29:31.729
You fatass.

629
29:31.729 --> 29:32.855
Why are you acting like this all of a sudden?

630
29:32.855 --> 29:35.399
- Sergeant Kang Chan Seok, please calm down. - So what if you go to Hanguk University?

631
29:35.399 --> 29:36.984
- So what? - Please calm down.

632
29:36.984 --> 29:39.946
- Why are you yelling at me? - Go. Hurry. Get out of here, now.

633
29:39.946 --> 29:42.156
- The company commander ordered me to... - Get out.

634
29:42.156 --> 29:43.877
I'm going home the day after tomorrow.

635
29:43.877 --> 29:47.078
You still have a long way to go in your service, you fat pig.

636
29:47.078 --> 29:48.861
Good hold.

637
29:58.923 --> 30:03.135
On September 18, 2.17 million won... 1.37 million won...

638
30:03.135 --> 30:05.806
Gosh... 41,000 won... 14,000 won...

639
30:05.806 --> 30:09.053
And two whole days with no sales at all...

640
30:12.145 --> 30:13.609
Hey.

641
30:14.256 --> 30:16.376
- Mr. Chairman. - What's going on?

642
30:16.376 --> 30:18.818
Is this really the time to be looking at the books?

643
30:18.818 --> 30:20.861
All 100 computers have been sitting idle for days.

644
30:20.861 --> 30:23.823
I won't even make enough to cover the ramen, let alone the electric bill.

645
30:23.823 --> 30:27.827
Do you know when they'll lift the restrictions on overnight passes, day passes, and leave?

646
30:27.827 --> 30:31.205
With the soldiers stuck on base, business is in the gutter.

647
30:31.205 --> 30:34.000
Come on, Mr. Chairman. You need to come up with a plan.

648
30:34.000 --> 30:38.546
Our motel has so many empty rooms, it'll be haunted soon.

649
30:38.546 --> 30:40.207
Hold on.

650
30:45.303 --> 30:47.888
Hey, it's me. Young Chul.

651
30:47.888 --> 30:51.600
Remember those three punks who caused that trouble?

652
30:51.600 --> 30:53.894
I need to see their faces.

653
30:53.894 --> 30:57.791
Tell them to get over to my restaurant right now.

654
31:00.443 --> 31:03.571
I'm Kim Young Chul,

655
31:03.571 --> 31:06.032
chairman of the Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association.

656
31:06.032 --> 31:08.325
You can count on me.

657
31:08.325 --> 31:10.953
[May this youth shine for the motherland!]

658
31:10.953 --> 31:12.830
Watch this.

659
31:12.830 --> 31:14.733
Hold it right there, sir.

660
31:17.501 --> 31:18.669
What brings you here?

661
31:18.669 --> 31:22.006
I'm Kim Young Chul, chairman of the Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association.

662
31:22.006 --> 31:24.342
I'm here to see the battalion commander,

663
31:24.342 --> 31:26.260
so open the gate.

664
31:26.260 --> 31:28.387
- Could you wait a moment? - A moment?

665
31:28.387 --> 31:31.223
You must be new here.

666
31:31.223 --> 31:34.462
All right. Well, this is new.

667
31:35.061 --> 31:38.811
Anyone here who doesn't know me is either a new recruit or a spy.

668
31:39.774 --> 31:42.360
- What is it? - Sergeant First Class Im. Long time no see.

669
31:42.360 --> 31:45.529
You're a hard man to catch.

670
31:45.529 --> 31:47.823
I've been busy. But seriously, what brings you here?

671
31:47.823 --> 31:50.571
I need to see the battalion commander.

672
31:51.285 --> 31:55.915
Given that unfortunate incident last time...

673
31:55.915 --> 31:58.667
Just open the gate, will you?

674
31:58.667 --> 32:01.045
You know we can't let you in without written authorization.

675
32:01.045 --> 32:02.797
Come on.

676
32:02.797 --> 32:05.508
We've known each other for years.

677
32:05.508 --> 32:07.468
Why would I need paperwork now?

678
32:07.468 --> 32:09.678
- My face is all the authorization you need. - Tell him to move the car.

679
32:09.678 --> 32:11.221
- Yes, sir. - Please move your car.

680
32:11.221 --> 32:12.223
What?

681
32:12.223 --> 32:14.392
This never happens...

682
32:14.392 --> 32:15.601
Just wait a minute.

683
32:15.601 --> 32:17.603
- I'll go take care of it. - Yes.

684
32:17.603 --> 32:20.456
Why are they suddenly being so...

685
32:21.046 --> 32:23.109
- What's going on? - Hey.

686
32:23.109 --> 32:26.195
Why are you being so strict today?

687
32:26.195 --> 32:28.781
The truth is...

688
32:28.781 --> 32:31.742
- I came to apologize. - Apologize?

689
32:31.742 --> 32:34.078
They might hear you.

690
32:34.078 --> 32:35.621
- Joon Young. - Corporal Yoon Joon Young.

691
32:35.621 --> 32:38.165
- He says he's here to apologize. - Seriously?

692
32:38.165 --> 32:40.835
Those looks on your faces are making me uncomfortable.

693
32:40.835 --> 32:43.379
Our sales have plummeted

694
32:43.379 --> 32:45.548
because of those overnight and day-pass restrictions.

695
32:45.548 --> 32:46.632
Oh, really?

696
32:46.632 --> 32:49.102
That's just terrible. What a shame.

697
32:50.344 --> 32:53.347
That sounds awfully sarcastic.

698
32:53.347 --> 32:55.307
Do I have to get on my knees

699
32:55.307 --> 32:58.769
- before you'll believe I'm sincere? - There's no need to kneel here.

700
32:58.769 --> 33:01.522
This is right in front of the guard post,

701
33:01.522 --> 33:03.190
so there's a lot of traffic.

702
33:03.190 --> 33:06.318
See that flower bed over there?

703
33:06.318 --> 33:07.695
That muddy spot?

704
33:07.695 --> 33:09.488
You can kneel there, mister.

705
33:09.488 --> 33:11.043
Mister?

706
33:11.043 --> 33:13.626
Come on. That's going too far.

707
33:13.626 --> 33:16.454
I'm Kim Young Chul, chairman of the Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association.

708
33:16.454 --> 33:19.457
And I'm Sergeant First Class Im Seong Min, the guard commander.

709
33:19.457 --> 33:20.957
- Tell him to move the car. - Yes, sir.

710
33:20.957 --> 33:22.856
Oh, come on...

711
33:23.586 --> 33:24.920
Hey, isn't this going to fall through?

712
33:24.920 --> 33:27.956
Just wait. I said I'll be done soon.

713
33:28.883 --> 33:32.344
Communication security. This is Sergeant First Class Im Seong Min, guard commander.

714
33:32.344 --> 33:33.566
Yes. Chungseong.

715
33:33.566 --> 33:35.807
Yes, understood. Yes. Chungseong.

716
33:39.810 --> 33:41.270
You're in luck.

717
33:41.270 --> 33:43.564
The battalion commander wants you to come up.

718
33:43.564 --> 33:45.608
Oh. Looks like it worked.

719
33:45.608 --> 33:49.153
I will never forget what happened here today.

720
33:49.153 --> 33:51.847
I'd appreciate that.

721
33:58.789 --> 34:01.332
This almost never happens. I don't know what's gotten into them today.

722
34:01.332 --> 34:02.917
What was that?

723
34:02.917 --> 34:05.085
You said we'd just come apologize and leave.

724
34:05.085 --> 34:06.879
They're busting our chops at the gate.

725
34:06.879 --> 34:10.591
We're still getting 100,000 won each, right?

726
34:10.591 --> 34:13.302
Of course.

727
34:13.302 --> 34:16.305
We're here now, so just do exactly what I tell you.

728
34:16.305 --> 34:18.516
- Got it? - Yeah.

729
34:18.516 --> 34:21.810
And try to look sorry, you punks.

730
34:22.478 --> 34:23.771
What was that soldier's problem?

731
34:23.771 --> 34:25.314
He was rude as hell.

732
34:25.314 --> 34:28.400
I've known that guy since he was a Staff Sergeant.

733
34:28.400 --> 34:30.502
He's always been like that.

734
34:32.028 --> 34:33.574
What?

735
34:38.160 --> 34:39.411
Halt.

736
34:39.411 --> 34:41.038
What is all this?

737
34:41.038 --> 34:42.961
Halt.

738
34:49.421 --> 34:51.590
Everyone out of the vehicle.

739
34:51.590 --> 34:53.342
I'm Kim Young Chul, chairman of the Yooncheon-ri...

740
34:53.342 --> 34:55.090
Exit the vehicle.

741
34:56.470 --> 34:58.764
What's going on here?

742
34:58.764 --> 35:00.933
Everyone out, now.

743
35:00.933 --> 35:03.894
Get out and put your hands above your heads.

744
35:03.894 --> 35:07.013
- Turn off the engine and put your hands up. - Turn off the engine...

745
35:08.274 --> 35:11.358
Suspected intruders spotted.

746
35:12.361 --> 35:14.496
Why are you doing this?

747
35:15.573 --> 35:16.824
Who are you?

748
35:16.824 --> 35:18.450
We're in the middle of an operation.

749
35:18.450 --> 35:20.578
Oh, you must be in charge.

750
35:20.578 --> 35:23.622
I'm Kim Young Chul, chairman of the Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association.

751
35:23.622 --> 35:24.885
I have an appointment

752
35:24.885 --> 35:27.042
- with the battalion commander... - The five-minute standby unit

753
35:27.042 --> 35:28.627
is conducting a live operation

754
35:28.627 --> 35:30.671
against a suspected intruder inside our perimeter.

755
35:30.671 --> 35:34.091
Until your identities are verified, no one may pass.

756
35:34.091 --> 35:36.051
You know who I am.

757
35:36.051 --> 35:38.429
I own the best barbecue restaurant in Yooncheon-ri...

758
35:38.429 --> 35:43.017
Regulations require us to search everyone on base.

759
35:43.017 --> 35:46.979
If you fail to respond to our challenge, we may fire live rounds.

760
35:46.979 --> 35:48.731
Live rounds? You'll fire?

761
35:48.731 --> 35:50.450
That's correct.

762
35:51.817 --> 35:53.027
Don't look at him.

763
35:53.027 --> 35:55.237
The weapon is loaded with live ammunition,

764
35:55.237 --> 35:57.448
so an accidental discharge is possible.

765
35:57.448 --> 35:59.700
Do not make any unnecessary movements.

766
35:59.700 --> 36:01.410
- Yes... - Don't move.

767
36:01.410 --> 36:04.622
Cha Byeong Ho, calm down.

768
36:04.622 --> 36:06.874
If there's another accidental discharge like last time,

769
36:06.874 --> 36:09.002
you'll get more than the stockade.

770
36:09.002 --> 36:10.252
Understood!

771
36:10.252 --> 36:13.130
Then... what can we do to cooperate?

772
36:13.130 --> 36:16.411
Intruders neutralized. Request permission to return.

773
36:16.411 --> 36:17.895
Copy.

774
36:17.895 --> 36:18.939
Staff Sergeant Choi.

775
36:18.939 --> 36:20.971
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok and Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam

776
36:20.971 --> 36:22.973
have neutralized the intruders and are on their way back.

777
36:22.973 --> 36:24.282
Okay.

778
36:27.519 --> 36:29.271
There they are.

779
36:29.271 --> 36:30.856
Move.

780
36:30.856 --> 36:32.869
Keep moving.

781
36:34.234 --> 36:36.822
Stop faking it, you jerk.

782
36:39.480 --> 36:42.034
On your knees.

783
36:42.034 --> 36:43.749
Get on your knees.

784
36:53.671 --> 36:56.215
[20 minutes earlier]

785
36:56.215 --> 36:57.758
Our guests are here.

786
36:57.758 --> 36:58.842
Get ready to welcome them.

787
36:58.842 --> 36:59.843
All right, attention.

788
36:59.843 --> 37:01.178
- Attention. - Attention.

789
37:01.178 --> 37:03.265
Operation Epic Fury,

790
37:03.265 --> 37:06.001
also known as Grand Fury.

791
37:06.001 --> 37:11.397
We're going to sear our fury into the chairman and those punks' bones

792
37:11.397 --> 37:15.275
and make them pay for looking down on soldiers.

793
37:15.275 --> 37:17.152
Before they set foot in the battalion commander's office,

794
37:17.152 --> 37:19.530
we'll scare them senseless and shake them to their core.

795
37:19.530 --> 37:21.573
- Do you understand? - Yes, sir.

796
37:21.573 --> 37:24.368
Chan Seok and Byeong Nam are key to this operation.

797
37:24.368 --> 37:25.786
Got it?

798
37:25.786 --> 37:27.830
As soon as those punks see your faces,

799
37:27.830 --> 37:31.333
they'll remember what happened last time and piss themselves.

800
37:31.333 --> 37:33.514
- Got it? - Yes, sir.

801
37:33.514 --> 37:34.544
- First Sergeant. - Yes.

802
37:34.544 --> 37:36.922
- Let's go brief the battalion commander. - All right.

803
37:36.922 --> 37:39.174
Chan Seok and Byeong Nam, go ahead and stand by.

804
37:39.174 --> 37:41.301
Ddong Il Gu, set up everyone else.

805
37:41.301 --> 37:42.177
Yes, sir.

806
37:42.177 --> 37:43.865
- Let's go. - Okay.

807
37:48.600 --> 37:50.269
Everyone, attention.

808
37:50.269 --> 37:51.937
- Attention. - Attention.

809
37:51.937 --> 37:54.523
What's the key to this operation?

810
37:54.523 --> 37:56.942
Looking intimidating.

811
37:56.942 --> 37:59.916
Everyone, look intimidating.

812
38:00.739 --> 38:02.280
Good.

813
38:02.906 --> 38:05.045
Im Da Hye, good.

814
38:05.701 --> 38:09.953
- Aren't you going to state your rank and name? - Corporal Im Da Hye. Sorry.

815
38:11.999 --> 38:13.041
Okay.

816
38:13.041 --> 38:14.334
Kim Sang Hun, good.

817
38:14.334 --> 38:16.170
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun. Thank you.

818
38:16.170 --> 38:19.173
Hold that look. Don't blink. Got it?

819
38:19.173 --> 38:21.766
- Yes, sir. - Good.

820
38:25.138 --> 38:26.706
Put some fire in your eyes.

821
38:28.348 --> 38:31.852
You're not even borderline intimidating. You're definitely not intimidating.

822
38:31.852 --> 38:33.073
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

823
38:33.073 --> 38:35.275
I look different without my glasses.

824
38:36.190 --> 38:37.483
Oh. Okay.

825
38:37.483 --> 38:38.996
Now you're definitely even less intimidating.

826
38:38.996 --> 38:40.360
Moon Bit Na Ri, fall out.

827
38:40.360 --> 38:41.403
Falling out.

828
38:41.403 --> 38:44.439
Good...

829
38:45.032 --> 38:46.585
Good...

830
38:48.786 --> 38:49.953
No Bat, fall out.

831
38:49.953 --> 38:51.246
I'm no joke, Staff Sergeant.

832
38:51.246 --> 38:53.081
Your expression looks too fake.

833
38:53.081 --> 38:54.917
Fall out and stand next to Moon Bit Na Ri.

834
38:54.917 --> 38:57.005
Yes, Staff Sergeant. Yoon Mo.

835
38:58.045 --> 39:00.299
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo, falling out.

836
39:00.299 --> 39:04.334
Good. I like the self-awareness, Sung Yoon Mo.

837
39:05.969 --> 39:08.620
We need one more...

838
39:12.421 --> 39:14.603
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo, falling out.

839
39:14.603 --> 39:18.740
Good. I like the self-awareness, Sung Yoon Mo.

840
39:20.317 --> 39:22.961
We need one more...

841
39:26.698 --> 39:28.992
Platoon Leader...

842
39:28.992 --> 39:30.994
May I ask you a favor?

843
39:30.994 --> 39:33.747
What kind of favor at a time like this?

844
39:33.747 --> 39:36.778
- Could you sit this one out? - Sit...

845
39:42.425 --> 39:44.591
I can't possibly be grouped with these men...

846
39:44.591 --> 39:46.718
I should play a pivotal role in neutralizing the intruders...

847
39:46.718 --> 39:49.638
Actually... this role is even more important.

848
39:49.638 --> 39:52.349
Only you can do it.

849
39:52.349 --> 39:53.392
Is that so?

850
39:53.392 --> 39:56.179
Then leave it to me.

851
40:02.401 --> 40:04.421
Easy... Be gentle.

852
40:05.072 --> 40:06.363
Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu...

853
40:06.363 --> 40:08.073
Isn't this just a prisoner-of-war exercise?

854
40:08.073 --> 40:11.285
This is the most important part of the operation.

855
40:11.285 --> 40:13.244
You need to play the intruder well,

856
40:13.244 --> 40:15.956
so we can set the right tone today.

857
40:15.956 --> 40:17.916
- Is that so? - Yes.

858
40:17.916 --> 40:20.002
Then, as the unit's resident mood maker,

859
40:20.002 --> 40:21.670
I'll set the tone perfectly.

860
40:21.670 --> 40:23.213
That's our platoon leader.

861
40:23.213 --> 40:25.307
Impressive.

862
40:26.550 --> 40:28.818
Claustrophobia.

863
40:30.095 --> 40:32.431
He hasn't even put the hood on you yet.

864
40:32.431 --> 40:33.515
What are you doing?

865
40:33.515 --> 40:35.957
I was practicing...

866
40:38.228 --> 40:39.813
Did the laundry not wash right?

867
40:39.813 --> 40:41.231
It smells...

868
40:41.231 --> 40:43.051
I can't breathe very well...

869
40:45.736 --> 40:49.283
This really makes me feel like an intruder.

870
40:49.283 --> 40:52.661
Even with a hood on, Bit Na Ri is unmistakably Bit Na Ri.

871
40:52.661 --> 40:55.329
What are you built like, an eight-foot aquarium?

872
40:55.329 --> 40:56.496
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri...

873
40:56.496 --> 40:59.082
If we do this a few more times, I think I'll lose all this weight.

874
40:59.082 --> 41:00.959
Enough. Setup complete.

875
41:00.959 --> 41:05.505
Now let's drag these intruders over there and finish them off for good.

876
41:05.505 --> 41:06.882
Kang Chan Seok, Choi Byeong Nam.

877
41:06.882 --> 41:08.760
Make it rough, like it's real. Got it?

878
41:08.760 --> 41:09.801
- Understood. - Understood.

879
41:09.801 --> 41:11.887
Finish us off? Rough?

880
41:11.887 --> 41:13.013
Nobody said anything about that.

881
41:13.013 --> 41:15.724
We're heading over, so have the knives, scissors and the blood ready.

882
41:15.724 --> 41:17.434
- Knives? - Knives?

883
41:17.434 --> 41:19.478
Knives and...

884
41:19.478 --> 41:20.312
Blood?

885
41:20.312 --> 41:22.981
Hey, Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu. Blood...

886
41:22.981 --> 41:25.025
- Knives... - Wait!

887
41:25.025 --> 41:26.401
- Hold on! - Why did you need...

888
41:26.401 --> 41:27.444
Staff Sergeant Choi.

889
41:27.444 --> 41:29.321
Sergeant Kang Chan Seok and Sergeant Choi Byeong Nam

890
41:29.321 --> 41:31.281
have neutralized the intruders and are on their way back.

891
41:31.281 --> 41:32.664
Okay.

892
41:35.911 --> 41:38.034
There they are.

893
41:41.083 --> 41:42.417
Move.

894
41:42.417 --> 41:44.576
Keep moving.

895
41:53.514 --> 41:55.555
Aren't they taking this brutality a little too far?

896
41:55.555 --> 41:56.890
On your knees.

897
41:56.890 --> 41:58.623
Get on your knees.

898
41:59.959 --> 42:02.293
Move and I'll shoot.

899
42:02.293 --> 42:05.029
Do we really have to go this far?

900
42:05.029 --> 42:06.441
Seriously... Again?

901
42:06.441 --> 42:08.860
Are you a soldier or a killing machine?

902
42:08.860 --> 42:10.626
I actually feel bad for the intruders.

903
42:10.626 --> 42:12.042
Hey.

904
42:12.042 --> 42:13.365
Don't feel like walking?

905
42:13.365 --> 42:14.449
Just say the word.

906
42:14.449 --> 42:15.993
I'll make you crawl for the rest of your life.

907
42:15.993 --> 42:17.953
Wouldn't that be hard on him?

908
42:17.953 --> 42:19.287
If you don't want to walk, just say so.

909
42:19.287 --> 42:21.918
I'll bury you in the mountains so you never have to walk or crawl again.

910
42:21.918 --> 42:23.293
Sit up straight.

911
42:23.293 --> 42:24.543
Please spare me.

912
42:24.543 --> 42:26.543
I don't want to be buried in the mountains.

913
42:26.543 --> 42:28.126
I don't want to become wild boar food.

914
42:28.126 --> 42:30.298
Take it easy.

915
42:30.298 --> 42:31.598
People are watching.

916
42:31.598 --> 42:33.093
Understood.

917
42:33.093 --> 42:34.177
But who are they?

918
42:34.177 --> 42:35.595
We're still verifying their identities.

919
42:35.595 --> 42:37.971
What? Are they intruders?

920
42:43.877 --> 42:45.605
Why are you trying to act tough?

921
42:45.605 --> 42:47.907
Watch how you look at me.

922
42:49.001 --> 42:50.318
Hey, what's wrong?

923
42:50.318 --> 42:52.490
Those are the soldiers from that day.

924
42:52.490 --> 42:56.306
- What are you talking about? - They're the ones we ganged up on...

925
42:58.710 --> 42:59.828
Don't move.

926
42:59.828 --> 43:01.288
What's gotten into you two?

927
43:01.288 --> 43:03.418
I told you not to get on these men's bad side...

928
43:03.418 --> 43:04.959
Excuse me...

929
43:07.209 --> 43:08.920
Lower your weapons.

930
43:08.920 --> 43:09.924
Lower them.

931
43:09.924 --> 43:11.798
- Understood. - Understood.

932
43:11.798 --> 43:13.800
Don't you know him?

933
43:13.800 --> 43:15.844
I'm sorry.

934
43:15.844 --> 43:17.012
Captain Cho.

935
43:17.012 --> 43:21.602
My heart is pounding so hard, I feel like I'm going to die.

936
43:21.602 --> 43:23.060
- You can put your hands down now. - Really?

937
43:23.060 --> 43:24.459
Yes.

938
43:24.459 --> 43:26.521
This is an active operation, so there was no choice.

939
43:26.521 --> 43:28.523
It's dangerous all the way to the battalion commander's office,

940
43:28.523 --> 43:30.859
so we'll escort you there. Let's go.

941
43:30.859 --> 43:32.376
I told you, there's no question who I am.

942
43:32.376 --> 43:34.418
Quiet.

943
43:34.418 --> 43:35.867
Follow him.

944
43:35.867 --> 43:37.949
- Keep moving. - Keep moving.

945
43:37.949 --> 43:39.543
- Eyes front. - Heads down.

946
43:39.543 --> 43:41.835
Eyes front. Keep moving.

947
43:41.835 --> 43:43.914
All right, get up. Get up.

948
43:43.914 --> 43:44.959
Don't drag your feet.

949
43:44.959 --> 43:47.838
If I hear them scraping, I'll shoot off every toe.

950
43:49.668 --> 43:51.723
I can see your feet.

951
43:53.006 --> 43:54.626
[Battalion Commander's Office]

952
43:54.626 --> 43:56.259
- Chungseong. - Chungseong.

953
43:56.259 --> 43:58.918
Battalion Commander, I've brought them.

954
43:58.918 --> 44:00.518
Please come in.

955
44:02.585 --> 44:03.992
Get in here.

956
44:04.705 --> 44:06.269
It's a little noisy out there, isn't it?

957
44:06.269 --> 44:10.649
Yes... It was pretty terrifying.

958
44:10.649 --> 44:12.969
- Have a seat. - Yes.

959
44:14.447 --> 44:18.168
Since you asked to see me, I assume you've settled everything?

960
44:18.168 --> 44:23.555
I'll make sure they're thoroughly disciplined so this never happens again.

961
44:27.251 --> 44:30.293
I don't think I'm the one you owe an apology to.

962
44:30.293 --> 44:33.835
The people who really deserve one aren't here yet.

963
44:33.835 --> 44:35.376
Come in.

964
44:40.459 --> 44:42.305
Chungseong. Love you.

965
44:42.305 --> 44:43.473
Chungseong.

966
44:43.473 --> 44:47.476
Aren't those the soldiers, the killing machines from earlier?

967
44:47.476 --> 44:49.117
- We're sorry. - We're sorry.

968
44:49.714 --> 44:53.567
We must've been out of our minds back then.

969
44:53.567 --> 44:57.403
We were nobodies who acted tough because we didn't know our place.

970
44:57.403 --> 44:59.533
Please forgive us.

971
44:59.533 --> 45:01.867
We were so scared earlier...

972
45:01.867 --> 45:05.460
I mean, so terrified that we couldn't even apologize.

973
45:05.460 --> 45:07.624
What we did was unforgivable.

974
45:07.624 --> 45:10.253
That's right. We're total lowlifes.

975
45:10.253 --> 45:11.950
We're truly sorry.

976
45:21.668 --> 45:23.850
- Hey, kids. - Yes?

977
45:23.850 --> 45:26.507
I'm glad you've realized it now.

978
45:27.893 --> 45:30.395
You'll be enlisting yourselves before long.

979
45:30.395 --> 45:32.763
Then you'll understand how we felt.

980
45:33.356 --> 45:35.550
- Understood. - Understood.

981
45:38.459 --> 45:40.365
- Hey. - Yes?

982
45:40.365 --> 45:42.908
I caused my share of trouble when I was your age.

983
45:42.908 --> 45:45.705
You think you own the place just because you can fight?

984
45:45.705 --> 45:47.725
But...

985
45:47.725 --> 45:49.456
things are different here.

986
45:49.456 --> 45:51.207
No matter how tough you think you are,

987
45:51.207 --> 45:53.501
the moment you come here, you're nothing.

988
45:53.501 --> 45:56.213
There's nothing you can accomplish with your fists here.

989
45:56.213 --> 45:58.967
So start living right from now on.

990
45:58.967 --> 46:02.660
Don't let your mistakes hold you back later and leave you with regrets like mine.

991
46:02.660 --> 46:04.221
Got it?

992
46:04.221 --> 46:06.014
Yes, sir.

993
46:06.014 --> 46:07.772
Don't call me sir.

994
46:07.772 --> 46:09.517
Just change your ways.

995
46:09.517 --> 46:11.102
Yes.

996
46:11.102 --> 46:12.437
Battalion Commander.

997
46:12.437 --> 46:16.066
On behalf of those boys and the Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association,

998
46:16.066 --> 46:19.513
I'd like to apologize once again.

999
46:23.948 --> 46:27.483
Mr. Chairman, let me say one thing.

1000
46:28.161 --> 46:33.091
We haven't put up with the merchants' disrespect

1001
46:33.091 --> 46:35.710
and price gouging because we're powerless.

1002
46:35.710 --> 46:37.671
It's because...

1003
46:37.671 --> 46:41.793
you're the very people we risk our lives to protect.

1004
46:41.793 --> 46:43.385
You're absolutely right.

1005
46:43.385 --> 46:48.459
This whole ordeal has taught me a great deal.

1006
46:48.459 --> 46:50.892
So...

1007
46:50.892 --> 46:56.356
The Yooncheon-ri Merchants Association has prepared something as an apology.

1008
46:56.356 --> 46:58.293
If you'll allow it,

1009
46:58.293 --> 47:02.480
we'd like to treat the troops to dinner tonight.

1010
47:05.450 --> 47:07.324
That won't be necessary.

1011
47:07.324 --> 47:12.084
But we prepared it as a sincere apology...

1012
47:12.084 --> 47:14.249
If you truly want to apologize,

1013
47:14.249 --> 47:18.042
show us common decency and respect instead of trying to compensate us.

1014
47:18.042 --> 47:20.709
Common decency and respect...

1015
47:20.709 --> 47:24.843
However, to prevent this from happening again,

1016
47:24.843 --> 47:27.518
promise me three things.

1017
47:28.179 --> 47:29.806
First,

1018
47:29.806 --> 47:33.393
abolish higher prices for soldiers at every business in Yooncheon-ri.

1019
47:33.393 --> 47:34.936
[For Military Only]

1020
47:34.936 --> 47:37.938
[Always 10% Off for Military Personnel] Charging soldiers more for the same food

1021
47:37.938 --> 47:40.442
[Free Upsize &amp; Dumplings for Military!] will no longer be tolerated.

1022
47:40.442 --> 47:41.568
[Regular: 15,000 won, Military: 35,000 won]

1023
47:41.568 --> 47:42.777
[Regular: 15,000 won, Military: 10,000 won]

1024
47:42.777 --> 47:44.029
[PC Room: 3,000 won per hour]

1025
47:44.029 --> 47:45.668
[PC Room: 1,000 won per hour]

1026
47:45.668 --> 47:46.710
What?

1027
47:46.710 --> 47:50.117
Second, if our soldiers face unfair threats,

1028
47:50.117 --> 47:54.539
personally step in to protect them and report the incident.

1029
47:54.539 --> 48:00.766
Stop exploiting the fact that our soldiers don't want trouble with civilians.

1030
48:01.548 --> 48:03.548
Third,

1031
48:03.548 --> 48:05.717
place a military-friendly certification mark

1032
48:05.717 --> 48:08.958
at the entrance of every restaurant and business in Yooncheon-ri.

1033
48:09.751 --> 48:10.930
Done.

1034
48:10.930 --> 48:13.301
Don't just say you're sorry.

1035
48:13.901 --> 48:15.657
Prove your respect

1036
48:16.257 --> 48:19.140
for soldiers through your actions.

1037
48:25.904 --> 48:27.628
Understood.

1038
48:28.287 --> 48:33.601
I'll personally take care of all three.

1039
48:35.041 --> 48:36.748
I'm counting on you.

1040
48:48.846 --> 48:52.972
Do you really think the soldiers will come?

1041
48:52.972 --> 48:55.311
The battalion commander gave his word,

1042
48:55.311 --> 48:56.668
so all we can do is wait.

1043
48:56.668 --> 48:57.918
What if they don't come?

1044
48:57.918 --> 48:59.722
Then...

1045
49:00.543 --> 49:03.869
I guess we'll all have to pack up and leave.

1046
49:07.028 --> 49:09.293
They're coming.

1047
49:09.293 --> 49:10.334
- What? - They're coming.

1048
49:10.334 --> 49:12.071
What's coming?

1049
49:18.042 --> 49:20.094
Chungseong. Love you.

1050
49:21.918 --> 49:24.209
They're coming.

1051
49:24.209 --> 49:25.334
- What? - They're coming.

1052
49:25.334 --> 49:27.026
What's coming?

1053
49:33.001 --> 49:34.501
Chungseong. Love you.

1054
49:34.501 --> 49:36.391
Sir, we're here for dinner.

1055
49:36.391 --> 49:38.459
Welcome.

1056
49:38.459 --> 49:40.019
- Come on in. - Please, have a seat.

1057
49:40.019 --> 49:41.964
Yes, come on in.

1058
49:45.482 --> 49:47.905
- Hello. - Sergeant First Class Im.

1059
49:47.905 --> 49:49.571
- Good evening. - Yeah.

1060
49:49.571 --> 49:52.501
All right, let's get ready.

1061
49:52.501 --> 49:55.309
Get those aprons on.

1062
49:58.121 --> 50:00.743
Thank you. I truly appreciate it.

1063
50:01.499 --> 50:03.668
Chairman, as you promised,

1064
50:03.668 --> 50:06.963
can we expect fair prices and top-quality service?

1065
50:06.963 --> 50:08.882
Don't you worry.

1066
50:08.882 --> 50:11.009
I'll grill all the meat myself today,

1067
50:11.009 --> 50:14.053
and pile the tables high with freebies.

1068
50:14.053 --> 50:15.555
Hey, what are you doing?

1069
50:15.555 --> 50:18.668
Go take orders from our valued soldiers.

1070
50:18.668 --> 50:20.209
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

1071
50:20.209 --> 50:21.686
Please, have a seat.

1072
50:21.686 --> 50:25.288
Escort them in. Let's get ready.

1073
50:35.376 --> 50:37.246
Slow down. What's gotten into you?

1074
50:37.246 --> 50:38.626
No one's going to take your food.

1075
50:38.626 --> 50:41.039
More pork belly coming up.

1076
50:41.039 --> 50:44.042
This one's on the house,

1077
50:44.042 --> 50:46.668
so eat as much as you want.

1078
50:46.668 --> 50:48.815
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1079
50:52.459 --> 50:53.959
Chairman.

1080
50:53.959 --> 50:56.721
This meat seems a lot better than what you used to serve.

1081
50:56.721 --> 50:59.098
Come on, Sergeant First Class Im.

1082
50:59.098 --> 51:03.144
This is what Yooncheon-ri hospitality is really like.

1083
51:03.144 --> 51:05.608
I feel bad about how I treated you before,

1084
51:05.608 --> 51:08.084
so I'm making it up to you today.

1085
51:08.084 --> 51:09.380
All right.

1086
51:09.380 --> 51:10.918
Excuse me, sir.

1087
51:10.918 --> 51:13.407
Can we get food to go?

1088
51:13.407 --> 51:16.241
- To go? - Our youngest is away at training,

1089
51:16.241 --> 51:18.076
so he couldn't come with us.

1090
51:18.076 --> 51:19.953
Min Seok, get some for Se Gye too.

1091
51:19.953 --> 51:21.371
He couldn't come because he's at an event today.

1092
51:21.371 --> 51:22.710
Understood.

1093
51:22.710 --> 51:26.293
Sure. Then before you leave...

1094
51:26.293 --> 51:28.544
Take it easy.

1095
51:28.544 --> 51:31.881
Don't disturb the soldiers while they're eating.

1096
51:31.881 --> 51:34.934
I'll go get more meat.

1097
51:36.042 --> 51:37.377
Sir...

1098
51:37.971 --> 51:42.100
I saw you apprehend that suspicious person, and I was really impressed.

1099
51:42.100 --> 51:45.019
I want to be a soldier like you someday.

1100
51:45.019 --> 51:47.209
Look at those eager eyes.

1101
51:47.209 --> 51:49.607
Don't worry. You'll end up in the army

1102
51:49.607 --> 51:51.357
whether you want to or not.

1103
51:52.026 --> 51:53.566
Come here, say ahh!

1104
51:55.543 --> 51:56.531
Thank you.

1105
51:56.531 --> 51:58.283
Please let me know if you need anything else.

1106
51:58.283 --> 52:00.243
What are you talking about?

1107
52:00.243 --> 52:02.459
You've never made a wrap for me.

1108
52:02.459 --> 52:05.584
Sir, more garlic over here.

1109
52:05.584 --> 52:07.799
Coming.

1110
52:13.084 --> 52:14.585
Thank you, sir.

1111
52:14.585 --> 52:16.137
Don't thank me.

1112
52:16.137 --> 52:18.344
I just followed your plan.

1113
52:18.344 --> 52:21.042
I'm so glad everything worked out.

1114
52:21.042 --> 52:22.185
Yes.

1115
52:22.185 --> 52:25.602
Thanks to you, even things that seemed impossible to change

1116
52:25.602 --> 52:28.175
are finally starting to change.

1117
52:28.175 --> 52:31.357
The plan was truly excellent.

1118
52:31.357 --> 52:32.609
They're my men,

1119
52:32.609 --> 52:34.704
so I put a lot of thought into it.

1120
52:37.407 --> 52:42.190
You're a good leader to your soldiers

1121
52:42.190 --> 52:45.955
and exactly the kind of officer the army needs.

1122
52:45.955 --> 52:48.291
Not at all. That's too generous of you.

1123
52:48.291 --> 52:50.061
- Let's have a drink. - Sure.

1124
52:53.588 --> 52:55.162
This looks so good.

1125
52:57.501 --> 52:58.877
This is so good.

1126
52:58.877 --> 53:00.261
It's hot.

1127
53:00.261 --> 53:02.618
The more I think about it, the angrier I get.

1128
53:03.308 --> 53:05.058
Keep moving.

1129
53:05.058 --> 53:06.376
Do you know what?

1130
53:06.376 --> 53:08.770
I was a force to be reckoned with out there.

1131
53:08.770 --> 53:12.007
I'm only lying low right now because I choose to.

1132
53:12.815 --> 53:15.530
Do you know why I held back?

1133
53:15.530 --> 53:19.447
According to Chapter 3-2 of the Infantry Tactics Manual,

1134
53:19.447 --> 53:23.579
a trained officer's lethal skills must only be used as a last resort.

1135
53:23.579 --> 53:24.793
This is delicious.

1136
53:24.793 --> 53:26.245
Using the outer edge of this hand,

1137
53:26.245 --> 53:28.206
you strike the third and fourth cervical vertebrae...

1138
53:28.206 --> 53:30.084
Did you or Bit Na Ri ever train in martial arts?

1139
53:30.084 --> 53:33.904
I earned a poom belt in taekwondo when I was in elementary school.

1140
53:34.625 --> 53:36.126
Wait, a poom belt?

1141
53:36.126 --> 53:37.382
So you do have some training.

1142
53:37.382 --> 53:38.424
Yes.

1143
53:38.424 --> 53:39.929
I used to box.

1144
53:39.929 --> 53:41.418
You did?

1145
53:41.418 --> 53:43.265
But it was just fitness boxing.

1146
53:43.265 --> 53:45.014
Then why didn't you lose any weight?

1147
53:45.014 --> 53:46.015
I'm sorry.

1148
53:46.015 --> 53:49.685
Corporal No Hee Jeong, did you ever train in anything?

1149
53:49.685 --> 53:50.751
Hey.

1150
53:50.751 --> 53:52.438
See this chin?

1151
53:52.438 --> 53:54.543
This chin is even more dangerous than cauliflower ears.

1152
53:54.543 --> 53:56.359
It's the chin of a real brawler.

1153
53:56.359 --> 53:58.444
No one dares mess with me when they see this.

1154
53:58.444 --> 54:03.459
Big arms and muscles are completely useless in a real fight.

1155
54:03.459 --> 54:06.165
Combat skills with actual lethal power...

1156
54:08.501 --> 54:10.877
Here's more meat.

1157
54:10.877 --> 54:12.193
Thank you.

1158
54:12.836 --> 54:15.172
Pick them up, Moon Bit Na Ri.

1159
54:15.172 --> 54:16.421
I'll bring you a new pair.

1160
54:16.421 --> 54:17.422
Would you like more ssamjang?

1161
54:17.422 --> 54:18.751
No, thank you. I'll get it myself.

1162
54:18.751 --> 54:19.959
I'll get it.

1163
54:19.959 --> 54:22.042
- Then I'll come with you. - Let's go together...

1164
54:22.042 --> 54:23.793
Sit down. Relax.

1165
54:23.793 --> 54:25.156
I'll get it.

1166
54:28.835 --> 54:30.668
Did he just talk down to us?

1167
54:30.668 --> 54:33.147
- He did. - Yes, he did.

1168
54:40.042 --> 54:42.251
- This meat is delicious. - It really is.

1169
54:42.251 --> 54:43.251
The meat is really good.

1170
54:43.251 --> 54:44.793
You don't often see pork belly

1171
54:44.793 --> 54:46.990
- with this kind of marbling. - You really don't.

1172
55:04.126 --> 55:05.845
Today was exhausting, wasn't it?

1173
55:05.845 --> 55:08.906
Not at all. I couldn't be happier.

1174
55:08.906 --> 55:11.395
It's been so long since we had this many customers.

1175
55:13.311 --> 55:16.898
The meat is incredible.

1176
55:16.898 --> 55:18.316
Thank you.

1177
55:18.316 --> 55:20.151
I may be old,

1178
55:20.151 --> 55:22.779
but I was terribly shortsighted.

1179
55:22.779 --> 55:25.948
Those young soldiers who come to our village

1180
55:25.948 --> 55:30.717
are someone's children, more precious to them than life itself.

1181
55:31.710 --> 55:35.332
But we were blinded by a few extra bucks...

1182
55:44.428 --> 55:48.596
Please treat our soldiers warmly,

1183
55:48.596 --> 55:51.668
with the same care you showed them today.

1184
55:51.668 --> 55:53.429
And...

1185
55:54.268 --> 55:57.480
Keep working hard

1186
55:57.480 --> 56:00.194
and enjoying your peaceful life.

1187
56:00.194 --> 56:02.733
That's all we ask.

1188
56:04.459 --> 56:06.774
I promise I will.

1189
56:07.543 --> 56:09.116
Battalion Commander.

1190
56:09.116 --> 56:10.952
I, Kim Young Chul,

1191
56:10.952 --> 56:14.288
swear on the night sky tonight.

1192
56:14.288 --> 56:17.291
As of this moment,

1193
56:17.291 --> 56:19.460
Yooncheon-ri is a military-friendly zone.

1194
56:19.460 --> 56:21.251
Thank you.

1195
56:21.251 --> 56:22.255
Thank you so much.

1196
56:22.255 --> 56:24.131
- Thank you. - Thank you.

1197
56:24.131 --> 56:25.834
I truly appreciate it.

1198
56:27.209 --> 56:29.543
Our meat has always been this good, you know.

1199
56:29.543 --> 56:31.178
Of course.

1200
56:32.974 --> 56:35.434
Attention. The battalion commander has issued an order.

1201
56:35.434 --> 56:36.519
Effective immediately,

1202
56:36.519 --> 56:41.585
all restrictions on passes and overnight leave for battalion personnel have been lifted.

1203
56:41.585 --> 56:43.376
Those leaving base this weekend

1204
56:43.376 --> 56:48.210
must submit their pass or overnight leave forms as usual.

1205
56:49.585 --> 56:51.158
Hey.

1206
56:51.158 --> 56:54.870
Lieutenant Colonel Byeon is really something else.

1207
56:54.870 --> 57:00.084
We offered to treat the soldiers to meat as an apology yesterday,

1208
57:00.084 --> 57:02.626
but he flatly refused.

1209
57:02.626 --> 57:04.084
Really?

1210
57:04.084 --> 57:06.841
His charisma was unbelievable.

1211
57:06.841 --> 57:08.217
I'm this old,

1212
57:08.217 --> 57:10.928
and I've never had my heart race like that.

1213
57:10.928 --> 57:14.835
Hyeok Jin rallied his men and put the squeeze on you once,

1214
57:14.835 --> 57:18.272
and Yooncheon-ri nearly collapsed in less than a week?

1215
57:18.272 --> 57:20.877
Don't even get me started.

1216
57:20.877 --> 57:24.710
Our sales dropped to one-tenth almost immediately.

1217
57:24.710 --> 57:28.821
The whole town was like a graveyard.

1218
57:28.821 --> 57:31.365
If one battalion commander can do that,

1219
57:31.365 --> 57:34.201
you know what I could do as the regimental commander, right?

1220
57:34.201 --> 57:35.661
Come on.

1221
57:35.661 --> 57:40.326
Why make such a terrifying joke?

1222
57:41.042 --> 57:42.293
You'd better behave.

1223
57:42.293 --> 57:44.923
Of course I will.

1224
57:48.344 --> 57:50.343
Gold is worth a lot these days.

1225
57:50.343 --> 57:51.385
Is this a ruby?

1226
57:51.385 --> 57:53.031
You must be busy. You should get going.

1227
57:53.031 --> 57:54.042
Yes.

1228
57:54.042 --> 57:56.644
I'll be on my way, then.

1229
57:56.644 --> 57:58.354
Chungseong.

1230
58:03.731 --> 58:05.434
I'll see you later.

1231
58:10.196 --> 58:12.209
That jerk Byeon Hyeok Jin...

1232
58:12.209 --> 58:15.159
He just had to defy me again?

1233
58:15.159 --> 58:16.994
Just cover this one up quietly.

1234
58:16.994 --> 58:18.621
Settle with them and put it behind us.

1235
58:18.621 --> 58:20.168
Sir.

1236
58:20.168 --> 58:22.249
One of our soldiers was injured.

1237
58:22.249 --> 58:24.458
How can we do nothing?

1238
58:28.714 --> 58:30.274
[Lieutenant Colonel Nam Joong Beom (47th Class)]

1239
58:32.668 --> 58:33.959
Hey, Joong Beom.

1240
58:33.959 --> 58:35.878
It's me.

1241
58:35.878 --> 58:37.890
Working hard?

1242
58:47.358 --> 58:49.543
[Weekend Pass and Overnight Leave Roster]

1243
58:50.918 --> 58:52.780
Corporal No Hee Jeong,

1244
58:52.780 --> 58:56.626
when are you taking the overnight leave that was canceled last time?

1245
58:56.626 --> 58:58.355
I don't know.

1246
58:59.168 --> 59:02.621
Do you have any idea how hard it is for a clerk to get overnight leave?

1247
59:09.046 --> 59:11.190
[Orders for the opposing force assignment and mission for the 2012 Hoguk Exercise]

1248
59:12.842 --> 59:13.929
Urgent...

1249
59:13.929 --> 59:18.381
Orders for the opposing force assignment and mission for the 2012 Hoguk Exercise?

1250
59:19.682 --> 59:22.101
Assigned unit, 45th Regiment,

1251
59:22.101 --> 59:24.376
7th Battalion, Second Company...

1252
59:24.376 --> 59:25.980
What is this?

1253
59:25.980 --> 59:29.251
- What's wrong? - Call the company commander right now.

1254
59:29.251 --> 59:30.894
Yes.

1255
59:31.569 --> 59:33.738
Exercise results will be reflected in command evaluations...

1256
59:33.738 --> 59:35.573
Communication security. Corporal Sung Yoon Mo speaking.

1257
59:35.573 --> 59:36.793
Could you put me through...

1258
59:36.793 --> 59:40.124
Yes, sir. We just received an email.

1259
59:41.579 --> 59:44.790
Your battalion has been on quite a roll lately.

1260
59:44.790 --> 59:51.780
You even brought those stubborn merchants to their knees.

1261
59:53.007 --> 59:55.258
It was all thanks to the troops.

1262
59:55.258 --> 59:56.468
Yes.

1263
59:56.468 --> 01:00:01.348
Your devotion to your men and your unity are remarkable.

1264
01:00:01.348 --> 01:00:05.060
At this rate, your battalion will definitely be

1265
01:00:05.060 --> 01:00:07.407
the division's spearhead in the Hoguk Exercise.

1266
01:00:10.418 --> 01:00:12.651
- The Hoguk Exercise? - Yes.

1267
01:00:12.651 --> 01:00:15.946
You know what kind of exercise it is.

1268
01:00:15.946 --> 01:00:19.793
It's the largest and most important field maneuver exercise of the year,

1269
01:00:19.793 --> 01:00:21.952
with the entire corps mobilized.

1270
01:00:21.952 --> 01:00:23.704
The division's reputation is at stake,

1271
01:00:23.704 --> 01:00:26.042
and it's crucial to command evaluations.

1272
01:00:26.042 --> 01:00:29.001
Especially that spirited Second Company...

1273
01:00:29.001 --> 01:00:30.965
Cho Baek Ho is the company commander, right?

1274
01:00:30.965 --> 01:00:33.649
I have very high expectations.

1275
01:00:34.585 --> 01:00:35.800
Regimental Commander,

1276
01:00:35.800 --> 01:00:38.001
large-scale field exercises like this

1277
01:00:38.001 --> 01:00:41.639
usually finalize their unit assignments several months in advance.

1278
01:00:41.639 --> 01:00:42.765
That's right.

1279
01:00:42.765 --> 01:00:45.142
But a slot opened up this time,

1280
01:00:45.142 --> 01:00:49.325
so I personally recommended your unit to the division commander.

1281
01:00:52.858 --> 01:00:56.378
[95th Division, 7th Battalion, 2nd Company: Opposing Force Assignment]

1282
01:01:01.793 --> 01:01:04.418
Is Second Company serving as the opposing force?

1283
01:01:04.418 --> 01:01:06.664
Yes. Is there a problem?

1284
01:01:06.664 --> 01:01:08.582
Isn't that mission usually assigned to reconnaissance units

1285
01:01:08.582 --> 01:01:10.042
or special assault regiments?

1286
01:01:10.042 --> 01:01:13.546
Regular infantry like us aren't equipped to serve as the opposing force

1287
01:01:13.546 --> 01:01:15.464
- in the Hoguk Exercise... - Hyeok Jin.

1288
01:01:15.464 --> 01:01:17.383
You're a capable man.

1289
01:01:17.383 --> 01:01:19.751
I've handed you the perfect opportunity.

1290
01:01:19.751 --> 01:01:22.504
You should focus on making the most of it. Don't you agree?

1291
01:01:25.140 --> 01:01:26.350
Sir...

1292
01:01:26.350 --> 01:01:29.061
Have I done something wrong?

1293
01:01:29.061 --> 01:01:33.760
- What? - Command evaluations are coming up soon.

1294
01:01:33.760 --> 01:01:35.904
Giving our battalion an impossible mission like this

1295
01:01:35.904 --> 01:01:37.740
makes it seem like you intend

1296
01:01:37.740 --> 01:01:40.281
- to give us the lowest possible score... - Hyeok Jin.

1297
01:01:40.281 --> 01:01:41.991
No one will notice you

1298
01:01:41.991 --> 01:01:44.285
if you keep doing the same routine exercises.

1299
01:01:44.285 --> 01:01:47.788
But if regular infantry outperforms even a reconnaissance unit,

1300
01:01:47.788 --> 01:01:50.332
how do you think the division commander will see you?

1301
01:01:50.332 --> 01:01:51.917
Your unit's morale is through the roof

1302
01:01:51.917 --> 01:01:54.753
after taking down the Merchants Association.

1303
01:01:54.753 --> 01:01:58.465
Use that momentum to prove yourselves once again.

1304
01:01:58.465 --> 01:02:02.877
I know you'll do an excellent job.

1305
01:02:02.877 --> 01:02:04.054
Regimental Commander... I mean, sir.

1306
01:02:04.054 --> 01:02:07.474
- This still seems a little... - It's already been reported to the division.

1307
01:02:07.474 --> 01:02:09.605
I'm counting on you.

1308
01:02:11.356 --> 01:02:13.135
Want to stay for dinner?

1309
01:02:16.400 --> 01:02:18.949
Prepare a meal in the staff dining hall.

1310
01:02:25.534 --> 01:02:28.370
[Days Later, Gyeonggi Mountain Training Site]

1311
01:02:38.543 --> 01:02:39.715
Stay alert, everyone.

1312
01:02:39.715 --> 01:02:40.758
All right, dismount.

1313
01:02:40.758 --> 01:02:42.635
- Dismount. - Dismount.

1314
01:02:42.635 --> 01:02:44.334
Stay sharp from this moment on.

1315
01:02:44.334 --> 01:02:45.501
- Understood. - Understood.

1316
01:02:45.501 --> 01:02:47.168
Watch your step.

1317
01:02:47.168 --> 01:02:48.599
Make sure you all get down carefully.

1318
01:02:48.599 --> 01:02:49.642
Form two lines.

1319
01:02:49.642 --> 01:02:50.959
No more smiling.

1320
01:02:50.959 --> 01:02:53.382
If I see teeth, you're dead.

1321
01:02:56.418 --> 01:02:57.883
Seriously...

1322
01:03:01.293 --> 01:03:03.008
What is that?

1323
01:03:20.585 --> 01:03:22.418
What are those guys?

1324
01:03:22.418 --> 01:03:24.001
Are they even human?

1325
01:03:24.001 --> 01:03:25.636
They're not human. They're Marines.

1326
01:03:25.636 --> 01:03:29.180
[Invincible Marines]

1327
01:03:29.180 --> 01:03:30.860
Marines...
